-9c7d-6cfcfb070291" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-2897c7e8-e654-5e2c-9d8f-9aae7cb64010" :answer-field/choices ["answer-2897c7e8-e654-5e2c-9d8f-9aae7cb64010"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2897c7e8-e654-5e2c-9d8f-9aae7cb64010" :answer/id #uuid "2897c7e8-e654-5e2c-9d8f-9aae7cb64010" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10\\,\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-83a10579-467e-5020-9446-f0bcbebf0762" :question/id #uuid "83a10579-467e-5020-9446-f0bcbebf0762" :question/math-academy-id "q-211195" :question/problem "Expressed as an improper fraction or mixed number in its lowest terms, $4\\times 1\\,\\frac{3}{5}=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we write $4$ as an improper fraction:\n\n$$\n4=\\frac{4}{1}\n$$\n\nWe also write $1\\,\\frac{3}{5}$ as an improper fraction:\n\n$$\n1\\,\\frac{3}{5}=\\frac{(1\\times 5)+3}{5}=\\frac{8}{5}\n$$\n\nNow, we can multiply the numbers. We multiply the numerators, and we multiply the denominators:\n\n$$\n\\frac{4}{1}\\times \\frac{8}{5}=\\frac{4\\times 8}{1\\times 5}=\\frac{32}{5}\n$$\n\nWe can also write this improper fraction as a mixed number:\n\n$$\n\\frac{32}{5}=6\\,\\text{R}\\,2=6\\,\\frac{2}{5}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b10f977b-2a53-50e5-8c32-10046dd36dee"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b10f977b-2a53-50e5-8c32-10046dd36dee" :answer-field/id #uuid "b10f977b-2a53-50e5-8c32-10046dd36dee" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-6211ee24-5f4c-5aea-a7fc-6134d3d66b84" :answer-field/choices ["answer-6211ee24-5f4c-5aea-a7fc-6134d3d66b84"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6211ee24-5f4c-5aea-a7fc-6134d3d66b84" :answer/id #uuid "6211ee24-5f4c-5aea-a7fc-6134d3d66b84" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{32}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-8cf2b8e2-2314-5e9d-b171-6805247e3cfc" :question/id #uuid "8cf2b8e2-2314-5e9d-b171-6805247e3cfc" :question/math-academy-id "q-211257" :question/problem "$1\\,\\frac{1}{8}\\times 8=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we write $1\\,\\frac{1}{8}$ as an improper fraction:\n\n$$\n1\\,\\frac{1}{8}=\\frac{(1\\times 8)+1}{8}=\\frac{9}{8}\n$$\n\n \n\nWe also write $8$ as an improper fraction:\n\n$$\n8=\\frac{8}{1}\n$$\n\nNow, we can multiply the numbers. We multiply the numerators, and we multiply the denominators:\n\n$$\n\\frac{9}{8}\\times \\frac{8}{1}=\\frac{9\\times 8}{8\\times 1}=\\frac{72}{8}\n$$\n\nFinally, we reduce the fraction to its lowest terms by dividing the numerator and denominator by $8:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{72}{8}=\\frac{72÷8}{8÷8}=\\frac{9}{1}=9\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-ce44bb81-1719-5324-9680-2e521758603f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-ce44bb81-1719-5324-9680-2e521758603f" :answer-field/id #uuid "ce44bb81-1719-5324-9680-2e521758603f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-c4b1c363-3d97-52db-ac92-bc64383e4842" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b5eda1c0-1f54-5820-bfb2-ec6dc216bc01" "answer-f355bedd-82be-5022-bfa7-014ed485cc9f" "answer-c107c182-10d5-5445-83ee-51f1cd8305b3" "answer-c4b1c363-3d97-52db-ac92-bc64383e4842" "answer-d009f007-1cef-5959-8edf-02da69c9184d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b5eda1c0-1f54-5820-bfb2-ec6dc216bc01" :answer/id #uuid "b5eda1c0-1f54-5820-bfb2-ec6dc216bc01" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f355bedd-82be-5022-bfa7-014ed485cc9f" :answer/id #uuid "f355bedd-82be-5022-bfa7-014ed485cc9f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8\\,\\frac{1}{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c107c182-10d5-5445-83ee-51f1cd8305b3" :answer/id #uuid "c107c182-1